WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.940
It's a new day on Tesla Short's time, episode 536, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.520
It's July 9th, 2026.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.760
Here's your Tesla news rundown.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:18.760
A U.S. judge's approval of the $1.5 million SEC settlement ends Musk's personal liability

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.620
in the 2022 Twitter Disclosure case.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:29.320
A U.S. judge approved a settlement between the SEC and Tesla CEO Elon Musk over late

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.540
disclosure of his 2022 Twitter share purchases.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:40.020
A trust in Musk's name will pay a $1.5 million fine, settling claims that the delay allowed

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:43.720
bargain purchases saving an estimated $150 million.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.620
The deal drops all claims against Musk personally and lets him state he was cleared of personal

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:53.340
liability without admitting wrongdoing.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.000
The penalty equals 1% of the alleged savings.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.860
The resolution removes a lingering legal overhang from Tesla's leadership while preserving

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:06.140
the ability to describe the outcome as a personal clearance.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.900
With one regulatory cloud lifted, Tesla is now focusing resources on product expansion in

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:13.960
its largest market.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:21.320
Tesla is launching a long wheelbase, 3-row L variant of the Model Y, aimed at U.S. growth.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.980
The move extends the current Model Y lineup with added seating capacity for the American

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:27.380
market.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:32.920
Production and pricing details remain tied to the broader U.S. expansion strategy.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:39.140
The variant directly targets family buyers seeking more interior space without shifting to

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.020
a new platform.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:46.700
This approach keeps capital focused on an existing high-volume vehicle rather than introducing an

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.080
entirely separate model.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:55.380
The same Model Y that is getting a U.S. specific stretch just reclaimed the top sales spot in China.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.340
The Model Y regained the title of China's best-selling vehicle in June.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:06.080
The result reflects strong monthly demand despite broader competitive pressure in the market.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:11.400
Tesla's position in China remains anchored by consistent Model Y volume.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:17.320
The monthly win demonstrates that the vehicle continues to outsell domestic alternatives

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.940
even as new rivals enter the segment with aggressive pricing.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:27.320
The permit price required to own a Tesla Model 3 in Singapore reached a new record high.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:32.520
The increase reflects tight vehicle quota limits and sustained buyer interest.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:38.520
Higher permit costs directly raise the effective price for new Model 3 registrations in the

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:39.260
city state.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:45.460
Buyers must now factor the elevated certificate of entitlement cost into any purchase decision,

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.420
tightening the economics for new registrations.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:54.740
Chinese automakers are reintroducing physical buttons after years of touchscreen heavy interiors.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.660
The shift reverses the minimalist interface direction Tesla popularized.

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:06.240
Regulators and consumer feedback on usability appear to be driving the change in the largest EV market.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:12.380
The policy reversal may influence how future Tesla interface updates are received in China

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:13.780
compared with other regions.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:21.320
Chinese EV exports rose 150% in the latest reported period, while Tesla recorded one of its

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:28.380
best monthly delivery totals of 2026. The parallel growth highlights expanding global supply

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:34.580
from multiple Chinese producers. Tesla's volume contributes to the overall export surge,

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:41.220
but faces increasing competition on price and range. The combined rise underscores how export

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:46.180
channels are becoming a larger outlet for both Tesla and domestic manufacturers.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.760
Real-world durability data may be helping sustain that demand.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:58.620
One Tesla owner has driven 247,000 miles while retaining enough battery capacity for 260

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:05.580
mile trips. The real-world data point shows degradation staying within usable daily range after nearly

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:11.040
a quarter million miles. The example adds to the growing record of long-term battery

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:16.620
performance under normal driving conditions. Such mileage figures provide direct evidence

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:23.000
that daily usability remains intact even after extensive use across varied climates and charging

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:30.040
patterns. High mileage battery data from individual Tesla's offers a clearer picture of real degradation

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:37.920
than any accelerated lab cycle can provide. A single car that has covered 247,000 miles while

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:44.640
still delivering 260 mile-range trips, supplies thousands of partial charge discharge events

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:50.780
under varying temperatures, speeds, and charging habits. That volume of uncontrolled data

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:56.180
points directly test the assumptions built into warranty reserves and residual value models.

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:02.500
The pattern of capacity retention after such extensive use supplies a benchmark that lab tests

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:09.200
alone cannot replicate. The practical consequence appears in how Tesla prices used inventory and

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:16.160
sets lease-end charges. When actual capacity loss stays within the band that still supports daily use,

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:22.160
the company can maintain tighter residual assumptions and lower the cost of ownership for the next

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:29.040
buyer. If degradation curves flatten more than expected, the same data also reduces the capital

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:36.200
Tesla must set aside for future battery replacements under warranty. Tesla data shows full self-driving

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:42.520
supervised consumes less energy than average human driving on the same routes. The smoother

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:48.000
acceleration and braking profiles produced by the software account for the measured efficiency gain.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:54.480
The finding adds a quantifiable operating cost benefit to existing FSD usage.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:01.220
Lower energy draw per mile can translate into reduced electricity expenses for drivers who enable

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:07.160
the feature regularly. Tesla has completed the planned supercharger installation in Albany.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:12.100
The site adds another high-speed charging location along key travel corridors.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:17.700
Local reporting confirms the station is now operational and available to drivers.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:23.600
The addition strengthens coverage on routes where drivers previously had fewer fast charging

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:29.840
options between major destinations. Efficiency gains matter most when charging infrastructure is

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:36.340
reliable. Tesla, Hyundai, and Kia are reducing the number of electric models offered in the United

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:43.760
States as overall EV demands slows. The pullback reflects weaker than expected sales across multiple

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:49.120
segments and forces manufacturers to concentrate remaining volume on higher selling variants.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.800
Tesla's adjustment focuses resources on core model Y and model 3 lines while trimming less

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:02.600
popular configurations. The consolidation aims to improve production efficiency and inventory turnover

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:09.620
during a period of softer overall demand. Use Tesla inventory is moving faster as buyers seek

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:16.160
lower operating costs amid fuel price pressure. The trend widens the secondary market for existing

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.540
owners looking to upgrade or exit. Higher turnover supports residual values for recent model

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:28.260
Teslas. Faster resale cycles can shorten the time owners hold vehicles before trading up,

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:36.040
indirectly supporting demand for new inventory. A new Chinese EV coupe priced at $22,000

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:40.540
features a semi-solid state battery pack and a dedicated makeup station.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:46.180
The vehicle targets younger urban buyers with lifestyle-oriented interior features.

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:51.920
Battery chemistry marks an incremental step beyond current liquid electrolyte cells in the segment.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:57.500
The combination of price point and specialized amenities positions the model as a direct

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:04.040
alternative in the entry-level coupe space. That market pressure is also visible in the aftermarket

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:10.260
and competitive moves. Tesla is actively building voice command support into full self-driving.

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:16.200
The feature would let drivers issue spoken instructions rather than screen taps during supervised

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:22.860
operation. Early testing focuses on common maneuvers and navigation changes. Integration

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:27.320
would reduce driver distraction while the car remains under active supervision.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:40.520
Aftermarket supplier unplugged performance is now delivering a 2.5-inch lift kit for the

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:46.300
current stance. Production and shipping have started, giving early cyber truck buyers an immediate

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:54.880
modification path. XPNG's Mona L03 is being marketed as a direct competitor to the entry-level

00:08:54.880 --> 00:09:01.660
Tesla Model Y. The vehicle combines competitive pricing with local market features aimed at younger

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:08.400
buyers. Its arrival adds another volume player in the segment Tesla currently leads in several regions.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:15.300
Hyundai and Kia's 800-volt EVs are experiencing roughly half the charging speed of native Tesla

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:21.540
vehicles at supercharger stalls. The speed difference stems from adapter and protocol limitations

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:27.880
rather than stall hardware. Owners of these models face longer dwell times when using the Tesla

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:35.580
network. Waymo is adding Robotaxi service in four additional US cities. The expansion increases

00:09:35.580 --> 00:09:42.140
the geographic footprint of its commercial driverless operations. The move widens the competitive set

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:49.160
Tesla's unsupervised FSD program while eventually face in multiple markets. Each new city adds

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:54.780
operational data and regulatory precedent that could shape future approval timelines for other

00:09:54.780 --> 00:10:03.180
autonomous fleets. Mercedes has introduced an all-new electric GLC SUV in China. The vehicle enters a

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:09.980
crowded premium SUV segment already contested by Tesla's Model Y and several domestic rivals.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:15.360
Pricing and range specifications position it as a direct alternative for buyers seeking

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:21.700
established luxury branding. The launch adds another established European nameplate to the list of

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:28.480
vehicles competing for the same family hauling buyers. Before we go, keep an eye on how the new Model Y

